    "license": "Project-authored adaptations of existing original project geometry, with original source/resource hashes and explicit transformations. Three.js 0.187.0 is MIT licensed, copyright 2010–2026 three.js authors. Preserve the pinned Three LICENSE and project lockfile for offline rebuilds.",
    "sourceDesign": "divided",
    "prompt": "Purpose: a real floor-standing makeup drawer host and four compatible drawer-installed storage payloads using the established company support, state, transform and save chain. Reuse pinned existing project sources with explicit editable adaptation parameters and identity instance scale. The host uses the original true sliding tray at Y minus .35m and a newly dimensioned .90 x .78 x .55m closed grounded carrier with actual connected rails and cavity. The four payloads retain the proven upper geometry and storage-roof, omit lower mechanisms and bake Y minus .09m without scaling. Preserve all common support patches, actual thick bottoms, walls, cup openings and case handles. Export deterministic self-contained GLBs and inspect actual loaded vertices, topology, contact, full-path fit and access through the new independent geometry gate. Keep each resource within 2500 triangles, 32 meshes and four materials. Reuse the proven upper outer walls, longitudinal dividers and left cross-divider around the shared contents patch. Retain real cell bottoms and at least two usable cells.",
    "sourceResource": {
      "id": "makeup-storage-divided",
      "version": 1
    },
    "method": "Reuse the pinned original storage generator upper structure and real storage-roof. Retain explicit upper prefixes, remove the lower carrier and slide, bake Y -.09 into original Float32 vertices, canonicalize near-zero base coordinates. No scaling.",
